\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Does the border-determinantal complexity of the m×m complex permanent grow at least c $m^{3}$ for one absolute $c>0$ and all sufficiently large m? Border complexity permits coefficient limits of affine-linear determinant representations.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Does the border-determinantal complexity of the m×m complex permanent grow at least c $m^{3}$ for one absolute $c>0$ and all sufficiently large m? Border complexity permits coefficient limits of affine-linear determinant representations.

